    "FIGARCH",
    "FIARCH"
  ],
  "conclusion": "SPY volatility exhibits significant long memory (GPH d=0.412 on |r|, d=0.359 on r\u00b2). FIGARCH(1,d,1) estimates d=0.610, confirming fractional integration. OOS QLIKE: FIGARCH=0.713229 vs GJR=0.762790 (-6.50%). DM test significant (p=0.0143). Hillebrand effect: GARCH persistence=0.9754 inflated to approximate fractional integration d=0.610. CAUTION: d=0.610 > 0.5 implies non-stationary long memory (between GARCH I(0) and IGARCH I(1)). This is theoretically possible but suggests the model may be closer to IGARCH than stationary FIGARCH. ANOMALY: GARCH (0.715649) beats GJR (0.762790) in OOS 2023-2024. This is unusual for SPY (which has strong leverage effect gamma=0.209). Possible explanation: 2023-2024 was a low-vol trending market where leverage asymmetry was less important. Period-specific, not generalizable. FIARCH has best OOS QLIKE but FAILS residual ARCH-LM (p=1.4963e-17), indicating remaining ARCH effects. Its OOS advantage is suspect. Best OOS model: FIARCH. SPY volatility has confirmed long memory (GPH d > 0.3, FIGARCH d > 0.5). However, this single-period OOS result contradicts prior work showing GJR as MCS-superior (full-sample AIC confirms GJR/EGARCH >> GARCH/FIGARCH). The OOS advantage of symmetric models in 2023-2024 is likely period-specific (low-vol trending market). Cross-OOS validation needed before any strong claims.",
